 Enabled: Yes\nWi-Fi Radio: OFF\nWi-Fi Connected: No","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":13,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:38:13.036804","tool_call_id":"call_eSIT6PConIwyfe7j94Nx4pE3","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":13,"usage":null},{"content":"It looks like my phone currently shows \"No Signal\" and \"Data Disabled\" in the status bar. Also, my device says there is no cellular service and the SIM card status is showing as missing. Because of this, I’m not able to make regular phone calls or use mobile data right now.\n\nWhat should I do next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":14,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:38:14.166276","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":14,"usage":{"completion_tokens":69,"prompt_tokens":2875}},{"content":"Since your phone shows \"No Signal,\" \"Data Disabled,\" and the SIM card status is \"missing,\" the first step is to reseat your SIM card. This means removing the SIM card from your phone and reinserting it to ensure it’s properly connected.\n\nPlease follow these steps:\n1. Power off your phone.\n2. Remove the SIM card from its slot.\n3. Wait a few seconds, then carefully reinsert the SIM card.\n4. Power your phone back on.\n\nAfter doing this, check if your phone now recognizes the SIM card and if you have cellular service. Let me know the results, or if you need guidance on how to remove and reinsert your SIM card.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":15,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:38:15.829349","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":15,"usage":{"completion_tokens":141,"prompt_tokens":6906}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":nu